      <tr> 
       <td style="width: 109px; height: 199px;" class=""><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Online Submission&nbsp;</span></strong></p><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">of Recommendation Letter</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 280px; height: 199px;" class=""><p class="1" style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Wednesday, September 2, 2026, 13:00</span></strong></p><p class="1" style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">–</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;Thursday, October 8, 2026, 17:00</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 392px; height: 199px;" class=""><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 8.4pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%; text-indent: -8.4pt; word-break: keep-all; text-align: justify;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">For graduate program applicants only; not mandatory but encouraged</span><br> <span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">(not for undergraduate applicants)</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 8.4pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%; text-indent: -8.4pt; word-break: keep-all; text-align: justify;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">The recommendation letter must be written by a professor from the applicant’s previous university. The recommender does not have to be the applicant’s academic advisor, but must be a professor who has taught or supervised the applicant, including retired professors. </span></p><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 8.4pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%; text-indent: -8.4pt; word-break: keep-all; text-align: justify;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">An email request for a recommendation letter (through the provided recommendation submission site) will be sent to the recommender when submitting an online application.</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 8.4pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-height: 130%; text-indent: -8.4pt; text-align: justify; word-break: keep-all;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">Only those recommendation letters submitted through the designated website will be accepted. (submission by post, email, fax will not be accepted)</span></p></td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr> 
       <td style="width: 109px; height: 114px;" class=""><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Submission of&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Materials&nbsp;</span></strong></p><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">showing artistic or athletic ability&nbsp;</span></strong></p><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">(by post or in person)</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 280px; height: 114px;" class=""><p class="1" style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Wednesday, September 2, 2026, 13:00</span></strong></p><p class="1" style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">–</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;Thursday, October 8, 2026, 17:00</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 392px; height: 114px;" class=""><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 9.8pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%; text-indent: -9.8pt; word-break: keep-all; text-align: justify;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -1pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">For applicants to the following departments only: College of Music</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt;">(excluding undergraduate Vocal Department and graduate Vocal majors (Voice, Choral Conducting))</span><span style="letter-spacing: -1pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">, College of Art &amp; Design, Division of Kinesiology &amp; Sports Studies, Content Convergence (Media Design)</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 8.4pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-height: 130%; text-indent: -8.4pt; text-align: justify; word-break: keep-all;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">Must be submitted to the International Student Affairs Team in person or by post. </span></p></td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr> 
       <td style="width: 109px; height: 67px;" class=""><p style="text-align: center;"><strong style="font-size: 12pt; text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Interview and Practical Exam</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 280px; height: 67px;" class=""><p style="text-align: center;"><strong style="text-align: center;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Saterday, October 24, 2026</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 392px; height: 67px;" class=""><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 9.8pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%; text-indent: -9.8pt; word-break: keep-all; text-align: justify;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -1pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">For applicants to the following departments only: College of Music(Voice and Choral Conducting)</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 8.4pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-height: 130%; text-indent: -8.4pt; text-align: justify; word-break: keep-all;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">Offline in-person audition(Zoom interviews are not available)</span></p></td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr> 
       <td style="width: 109px; height: 64px;" class=""><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Announcement of&nbsp;</span></strong></p><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Preliminary Admissions Desicions</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 280px; height: 64px;" class=""><p style="text-align: center;"><strong style="text-align: center;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"><br></span></strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong style="text-align: center;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Friday, November 13, 2026</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 392px; height: 64px;" class=""><p class="1" style="line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="text-indent: -8.4pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="text-indent: -8.4pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">Announcement of Preliminary Admissions Decisions: International Student Affairs Team website (</span><a href="http://isa.ewha.ac.kr" style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: 0pt; text-indent: -8.4pt;"><u><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt; color: rgb(128, 0, 128);">isa.ewha.ac.kr</span></u></a><span style="text-indent: -8.4pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">) &gt; Admissions &gt; Announcements</span></p></td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr> 
       <td style="width: 109px; height: 278px;" class=""><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Submission of Original</span><span style="font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;Documents</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 280px; height: 278px;" class=""><p class="1" style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Monday, November 16, 2026, 9:00</span></strong></p><p class="1" style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">–</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;Friday, November 27, 2026, 17:00</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 392px; height: 278px;" class=""><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 8.4pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%; text-indent: -8.4pt; word-break: keep-all; text-align: justify;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">Upon being offered preliminary admission, original hard copies of documents uploaded during the application period must be submitted in person or by post.</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 17.9pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%; text-indent: -17.9pt; word-break: keep-all; text-align: justify;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">- Applicants are advised to have all documents prepared in advance so that they can be sent promptly after the preliminary admissions decisions are announced.</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 17.9pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%; text-indent: -17.9pt; word-break: keep-all; text-align: justify;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;"> </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">Complete or partial failure to submit original documents may result in revocation of preliminary admission.</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 17.9pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-height: 130%; text-indent: -17.9pt; text-align: justify; word-break: keep-all;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;"> </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">Applicants who are expected to a) obtain a TOPIK score (level 4 or above) or b) complete a Korean language program (level 4 or above) at a Korean language institute: If offered preliminary admission, you must submit your TOPIK score report of level 4 or above or completion certificate of level 4 or above via email (</span><a href="mailto:isadmit@ewha.ac.kr"><u style="text-underline:#0000ff single"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">isadmit@ewha.ac.kr</span></u></a><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt;">) by Friday, November 27th, Failure to submit them will result in revocation of preliminary admission.</span></p></td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr> 
       <td style="width: 109px; height: 106px;" class=""><p style="text-align: center;"><strong style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Conditional Language Certificatr Submission (TOPIK)</span></strong></p><p class="1" style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p></td> 
       <td style="width: 280px; height: 106px;" class=""><p style="text-align: center;"><strong style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Thursday, Decamber 10, 2026</span></strong></p><p class="1" style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">–</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;Friday,</span></strong><strong style="font-size: 12pt; letter-spacing: 0pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Decamber 11</span></strong><strong><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">, 2026, 24:00</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 392px; height: 106px;" class=""><p style="margin: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">•</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">Only applicable to those who meet the TOPIK Level 4</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">&nbsp;qualification requirements</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">Please be sure to send your application to the&nbsp;</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">International Student Team via email (isadmit@ewha.ac.kr ) within the deadline&nbsp;</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">It must be submitted to. If it cannot be submitted, the preliminary acceptance will be revoked.</span></p></td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr> 
       <td style="width: 109px; height: 153px;" class=""><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Final Admissions &amp; Scholarship Decisions Announced Conditional Language Certificate Submission</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 280px; height: 153px;" class=""><p style="text-align: center;"><strong style="text-align: center;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Friday,</span></strong><strong style="font-size: 12pt; letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: center;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Decamber 18</span></strong><strong style="text-align: center;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">, 2026, 24:00</span></strong></p><p class="1" style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p></td> 
       <td style="width: 392px; height: 153px;" class=""><p style="margin: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 130%;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt;">•</span><span style="font-size: 9.5pt;"> </span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">Announcement of Final Admissions Decisions:&nbsp; &nbsp;International Student Affairs Team website (</span><a href="http://isa.ewha.ac.kr"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">isa.ewha.ac.kr</span></a><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">) &gt; Admissions &gt; Announcements</span></p><p style="margin: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-height: 130%;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">• </span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">Applicants who are offered final admission must&nbsp; &nbsp;carefully read the notice for accepted students and&nbsp; &nbsp;proceed with the necessary steps for enrollment and&nbsp; &nbsp;visa issuance, such as the submission of the&nbsp; &nbsp;statement of intent to register, submission of final&nbsp; &nbsp;academic documents and proof of financial ability,&nbsp; &nbsp;tuition payment, etc.</span></p></td> 
      </tr> 
      <tr> 
       <td style="width: 109px; height: 53px;" class=""><br><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Enrollment</span></strong></p><p style="line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">(Tuition Payment)</span></strong><br></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 280px; height: 53px;" class=""><p class="1" style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">January 2027</span></strong></p></td> 
       <td style="width: 392px; height: 53px;" class=""><p class="1" style="letter-spacing: 0pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">• Detailed instructions on payment period and&nbsp; &nbsp;procedures will be provided through the notice for&nbsp; &nbsp;accepted students by email.</span></span></p></td> 
      </tr> 
     </tbody> 
    </table> 
    <p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p> 
   </div> 
  </div> 
  <p>&nbsp;</p> 
 </div> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj461" style=""> 
 <h2 class="objHeading_h2"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 14pt;">&nbsp;Ⅱ</span>. Eligibility</h2> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj465" style=""> 
 <h6 class="objHeading_h6">&nbsp; To be eligible to apply, applicants must meet all the requirements below.</h6> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj466" style=""> 
 <h3 class="objHeading_h3">Nationality : Non-Korean*</h3> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objTag" id="menu1442_obj467" style=""> 
 <div class="objTag"> 
  <p><span style="font-size: 10pt;">※ Applicants and their parents must be nationals(i.e.passport holders) of a country other than Korea.<br><span style="font-size: 10pt;"> ※ Ewha Womans University accepts applications from female applicants only.</span> </span></p> 
  <p>&nbsp;</p> 
 </div> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj468" style=""> 
 <h3 class="objHeading_h3">Education: Applicants to each program must meet the academic requirements below</h3> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objTag" id="menu1442_obj469" style=""> 
 <div class="objTag"> 
  <table class="over_tbl en_tbl" style="height: 407.67px;"> 
   <colgroup> 
    <col width="20%"> 
    <col width="20%"> 
    <col width="60%"> 
   </colgroup> 
   <thead> 
    <tr> 
     <th colspan="2" scope="col" class=""><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Programs</span></th> 
     <th scope="col" class=""><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Eligibility</span></th> 
    </tr> 
   </thead> 
   <tbody> 
    <tr> 
     <td style="height: 283.68px;" rowspan="2" class=""><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Undergraduate Program</span></td> 
     <td class=""><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Freshman</span></td> 
     <td class="alignL"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Applicants who have graduated or are expected to graduate from high school <u>by Febrary 2027</u></span><br><span style="font-size: 10pt;"> ※ GED, Korean High school Graduate Equivalency Test, home schooling, cyber schooling, or other high school equivalency certificates are not considered as high school diploma. </span></td> 
    </tr> 
    <tr> 
     <td style="height: 186.68px;" class=""><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Transfer</span></td> 
     <td class="alignL" style="height: 186.68px;"><p><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Applicants who fall under one of the two cases below:</span></p><p><span style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 0pt; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">①</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">App</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">licants who have a) completed or are expected to complete at least 2 academic years (4 regular semesters, excluding summer/winter sessions) <em>and&nbsp; </em>b) earned at least half (two thirds in case of three-year British universities) of the minimum number of credits required for graduation at a four-year university&nbsp;</span></span><u style="font-size: 13.3333px;">by Febrary 2027</u></p><p class="0"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt;">② Applicants who have acquired or are expected to acquire an associate degree at a junior college&nbsp;</span></span></span><u style="font-size: 13.3333px;">by Febrary 2027</u></p><p style="line-height: 1.2;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;"><span>※ GED, Korean High school Graduate Equivalency Test, home schooling, cyber schooling, or other school equivalency certificates are not considered as school diploma. </span></span></p></td> 
    </tr> 
    <tr> 
     <td style="height: 71px;" rowspan="2" class=""><p style="line-height: 1.2;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Graduate Program</span></p></td> 
     <td class=""><p style="line-height: 1.2;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Master’s,<br>Combined Master’s</span><br><span style="font-size: 10pt;">and Doctoral</span></p></td> 
     <td class="alignL"><p style="line-height: 1.2;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Applicants who have acquired or are expected to acquire a Bachelor’s degree&nbsp;</span><u style="font-size: 13.3333px;">by Febrary 2027</u></p></td> 
    </tr> 
    <tr> 
     <td style="height: 20px;" class=""><p style="line-height: 1.2;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Doctoral</span></p></td> 
     <td class="alignL" style="height: 20px;"><p style="line-height: 1.2;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Applicants who have acquired or are expected to acquire a Master’s degree&nbsp;</span><u style="font-size: 13.3333px;">by Febrary 2027</u></p></td> 
    </tr> 
   </tbody> 
  </table> 
  <p class="0" style="line-height: 1.2; text-indent: -12.8pt; letter-spacing: -0.7pt; margin-left: 12.8pt; pagination: none; padding-alt: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0pt; font-width: 100%; text-raise: 0pt;">&nbsp;</p> 
  <span style="font-size: 10pt;">※ Students who are expected to graduate must graduate <u>by Febrary 28, 2027</u> and submit their authenticated graduation certificate before the start of the semester (or by one month before the start of the semester for those preparing for visa issuance and entry from abroad) to be eligible for admission.</span> 
  <p>&nbsp;</p> 
 </div> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj470" style=""> 
 <h3 class="objHeading_h3">Language Proficiency: Applicants must meet one of the following language proficiency requirements</h3> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objTag" id="menu1442_obj476" style=""> 
 <div class="objTag"> 
  <strong style="font-size: 10pt;">A. Undergraduate Freshman Applicants</strong> 
  <span style="font-size: 10pt;">:&nbsp;<strong><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">No language proficiency requirement</span></strong></span> 
  <div> 
   <span style="font-size: 13.3333px; letter-spacing: -0.666667px;">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span> 
   <span style="font-size: 13.3333px; letter-spacing: -0.666667px; text-indent: -28.6667px;">※&nbsp;</span> 
   <span style="font-size: 9.5pt; letter-spacing: -0.7pt; text-indent: -12pt;">Starting from the 2025 academic year, all incoming freshmen (except those in the Division of International Studies and the College of Nursing) will&nbsp;</span> 
  </div> 
  <div> 
   <span style="font-size: 9.5pt; letter-spacing: -0.7pt; text-indent: -12pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; automatically be enrolled in the Global Scholars Program within the HOKMA College of General Education. As part of this program, students must take&nbsp;</span> 
  </div> 
  <div> 
   <span style="font-size: 9.5pt; letter-spacing: -0.7pt; text-indent: -12pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Korean language and required liberal arts courses for at least one year (two semesters) upon admission. Students with a TOPIK level below 3 will be&nbsp;</span> 
  </div> 
  <div> 
   <span style="font-size: 9.5pt; letter-spacing: -0.7pt; text-indent: -12pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; restricted from enrolling in major-specific courses.</span> 
  </div> 
  <div> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 12pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -12pt; word-break: keep-all;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.666667px; text-indent: -28.6667px;">&nbsp; ※&nbsp;</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.7pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">To advance to their respective majors, students must first complete one year (two semesters) of study in the Global Scholars&nbsp;</span></p> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 12pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -12pt; word-break: keep-all;"><span style="text-indent: -12pt; letter-spacing: -0.7pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Program </span><u style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: 0pt; text-indent: -12pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.7pt; font-style: italic; font-size: 9.5pt;">and</span></u><span style="text-indent: -12pt; letter-spacing: -0.7pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"> </span><span style="text-indent: -12pt; letter-spacing: -0.7pt; font-size: 9.5pt;">obtain a TOPIK level of 3 or higher, or an equivalent qualification.</span></p> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 12pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -12pt; word-break: keep-all;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.7pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"><br></span></p> 
  </div> 
  <div> 
   <div> 
    <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 21.5pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -21.5pt; word-break: keep-all; letter-spacing: -0.5pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp; However, Applicants to Division of International Studies(International Studies,&nbsp;</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -21.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">Global Korean Studies)&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -21.5pt;">meet one or more of the English requirements below</span></p> 
    <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 21.5pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -21.5pt; word-break: keep-all; letter-spacing: -0.5pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -12.6pt; font-size: 10pt;">①</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -21.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; English Proficiency Test Scores: TOEFL iBT 80</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -10pt; font-size: 10pt;">(If the exam is taken after January 21st, 2026, 4.0)</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -21.5pt;">, IELTS 6.0, New Teps 326 or above</span></p> 
    <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 21.5pt; vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: 0pt; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -21.5pt; word-break: keep-all;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -10pt; font-size: 10pt;">②</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -21.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; Completion of high school education conducted entirely in English</span></p> 
   </div> 
   <div>
     &nbsp; 
   </div> 
   <div> 
    <strong><span style="">B.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;<span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-align: center; text-indent: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">Undergraduate Program (Transfer) &amp; Graduate Program :</span></span></strong> 
   </div> 
   <div> 
    <strong><span style="font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp; : At least one of the following l<span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">anguage proficiency requirements</span></span></strong> 
   </div> 
   <div> 
    <span style="font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"><br></span> 
   </div> 
   <div> 
    <span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; </span> 
    <span style="font-size: 13.3333px; letter-spacing: -0.666667px; text-align: justify; text-indent: -16.8px;">①</span> 
    <span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt;">&nbsp;TOPIK Level 4 or above</span> 
   </div> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp;※ </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">Accepted TOPIK: The 108th(test date: October 18</span><span style="font-size: 9.5pt; letter-spacing: -0.6pt; text-indent: 0pt;">, 2026)</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt;">&nbsp;or earlier&nbsp;</span></p> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Accepted TOPIK IBT: The 15th (test date:&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 13.3333px; letter-spacing: -0.666667px;">October</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;24</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.8px;">, 2026</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt;">) or earlier</span></p> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt; text-indent: 0pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; word-break: keep-all; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.3333px; letter-spacing: -0.666667px; text-indent: -13.3333px;">&nbsp; &nbsp;②</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">Completion of a Korean Language Program (Level 4 or above) at a Korean&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt;">language institute&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: 0pt;">affiliated with a university in Korea</span></p> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 28pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -28pt; word-break: keep-all; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp;※ </span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">Applicants who can complete level 4 or above by Novemver 27, 2026 are also eligible.</span></p> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 28pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -28pt; word-break: keep-all; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp;③&nbsp; English Proficiency Test Scores: TOEFL iBT 80</span><span style="font-size: 13.3333px; letter-spacing: -0.666667px; text-indent: -13.3333px;">(If the exam is taken after January 21st, 2026, 4.0)</span><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">, IELTS 6.0, New TEPS 326 or&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -28pt;">above</span></p> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 28pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -28pt; word-break: keep-all; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp;④&nbsp; Completion of high school or university education conducted entirely in Korean&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -28pt;">or English</span></p> 
   <p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 28pt; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 140%; text-indent: -28pt; word-break: keep-all; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 9.5pt;"><span style="letter-spacing: -0.5pt; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp; &nbsp;⑤&nbsp; Ewha's recognition that the applicant's level of Korean or English proficiency is&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; text-indent: -28pt;">equivalent to or higher than the above A~D requirements</span></p> 
  </div> 
  <p>&nbsp;</p> 
 </div> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj477" style=""> 
 <h2 class="objHeading_h2">&nbsp;Ⅲ. Selection Process</h2> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj479" style=""> 
 <h3 class="objHeading_h3">Selection Process:<br></h3> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objTag" id="menu1442_obj480" style=""> 
 <div class="objTag"> 
  <p><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Applicants will be selected through a comprehensive evaluation of their academic capability, language proficiency, preparedness in the chosen major, academic motivation, etc. shown in their submitted materials.</span></p> 
  <span style="font-size: 10pt;"> ※&nbsp;</span> 
  <span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; text-indent: 0pt;">Some applicants may be contacted individually for a phone or video interview if necessary.</span> 
  <p>&nbsp;</p> 
 </div> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj481" style=""> 
 <h3 class="objHeading_h3">Application Fee: 150,000 KRW (150 USD)</h3> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objTag" id="menu1442_obj482" style=""> 
 <div class="objTag"> 
  <p><span style="font-size: 10pt;">※ Applicants must complete payment of the application fee in order to submit their online application.</span></p> 
 </div> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objHeading" id="menu1442_obj483" style=""> 
 <h2 class="objHeading_h2"><span style="letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 14pt;">&nbsp;Ⅳ</span>. Required Documents</h2> 
</div> 
<div class="_obj _objTag" id="menu1442_obj484" style=""> 
 <div class="objTag"> 
  <ol class="alignL"> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">[Form 1] Application Form&nbsp;</span></li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">[Form 2-1] Personal Statement (Required for undergraduate program applicants Only)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; [Form 2-2] Study Plan (Required for graduate program applicants Only)</span></li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">[Form 3] Letter of Recommendation (For graduate program applicants only; not mandatory but encouraged)</span></li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">[Form 4] Scholarship Application (For Scholarship Applicants Only)</span></li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Certificate of (Expected) Graduation and Official Transcript of Academic Records</span>&nbsp;</li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Language Proficiency Test Score Reports or Certificates</span></li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Passport – Applicant and both Parents (Documents verifying Nationality)</span></li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Legal document verifying relationship between applicant and both parents</span></li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 13.3333px;">Supplemental materials</span></li> 
   <li><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Materials showing artistic or athletic Ability</span></li> 
  </ol> 
  <p><span style="font-size: 13.33px;"><br></span></p> 
  <p><span style="font-size: 10pt;">Enquiries: <span style="color: rgb(35, 35, 255); font-size: 10pt;"><u style="font-size: 10pt;">isadmit@ewha.ac.kr</u></span></span></p> 
 </div> 
</div>
		
	</article>
	
	
	















</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div id="_wrapFooter">
				<footer id="_footer">
